    "notes": "TWO adapter lifetimes over one --state-dir: run0 is the wallet as recorded, and the crawl of it writes seen.json; run1 is the counterfactual, and only what run1 emits is declared here. See adapters/bitcoin/corpus/reorg/RECORDED.md for exactly what run1 changes and why it had to be synthesized -- a real chain does not reorg on request. The spend 6d483d10.. is gone from run1's listing AND its direct GET /tx/:txid answers 404, and it is the 404 that makes it a tombstone: absence from a listing is never evidence. The tombstone carries the delta seen.json recorded (-60000), not a fabricated zero, and reason reorged_out rather than dropped_from_mempool because the state file says it was in a block. The balance moves with it: run1's chain_stats no longer record the spend, so confirmed is 60000 again. btc_fetch_fail is the other half of this rule -- the same absence with no 404 behind it, producing no tombstone at all."
